{"architectures":["arm64","x64","x86"],"id":"Rustlang.Rust.MSVC","latestVersion":"1.99.1","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"description":"A language empowering everyone to build reliable and efficient software.","license":"Apache-2.0 AND MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/HEAD/COPYRIGHT","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"description":"A language empowering everyone to build reliable and efficient software.","license":"Apache-2.0 AND MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/HEAD/COPYRIGHT","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"The Rust programming language helps you write faster, more reliable software. High-level ergonomics and low-level control are often at odds in programming language design; Rust challenges that conflict. Through balancing powerful technical capacity and a great developer experience, Rust gives you the option to control low-level details (such as memory usage) without all the hassle traditionally associated with such control.","moniker":"rust-msvc","name":"Rust (MSVC)","packageUrl":"https://www.rust-lang.org/","publisher":"The Rust Project Developers","publisherUrl":"https://www.rust-lang.org/","tags":["cargo","clippy","llvm","msvc","rust","rustc","rustdoc","rustup","windows"]}},"longDescription":"The Rust programming language helps you write faster, more reliable software. High-level ergonomics and low-level control are often at odds in programming language design; Rust challenges that conflict. Through balancing powerful technical capacity and a great developer experience, Rust gives you the option to control low-level details (such as memory usage) without all the hassle traditionally associated with such control.","moniker":"rust-msvc","name":"Rust (MSVC)","packageUrl":"https://www.rust-lang.org/","publisher":"The Rust Project Developers","publisherUrl":"https://www.rust-lang.org/","tags":["cargo","clippy","llvm","msvc","rust","rustc","rustdoc","rustup","windows"]},"schemaVersion